  cal-20261002-s2-074,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Were my 100% answers wishes about what I want rather than credences?,Four of them endorsed my own plans.,re-ask the 100% items as forecasts of what I will do,treat them as credences,calibration,78,55,82,75,78,exploit,Unresolvable automatically; resolved by this answer and the re-asked forecasts.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-043,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is 'I trust automated checks over my own spot checks' a stable pattern in my answers?,"12% on outrunning verification, 22% on needing human labels, 78% that review is ceremony.",add it as a second candidate effective variable,leave it out,synthesis,80,55,85,75,75,explore,"Resolved by a later #calibrator note naming it as an effective variable, or rejecting it, after session 3.",third session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-090,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would I notice within a week if a deploy broke a visualisation nobody else uses?,29% that anyone else uses the site; deploys are verified by agents.,rely on CI and Stage B,add one browser check per deploy,synthesis,72,62,75,80,75,explore,Resolved false if a later note reports a broken visualisation found more than a week after its deploy; true if one is found within a week.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-097,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Will Saka, Groß or Haaland be flagged injured before the 10 October deadline?",The international break has already injured Brobbey and Havertz; Palmer withdrew.,"confirm the squad on 9 October, not 7 October",lock the squad on 7 October,news,65,72,70,55,82,exploit,"Resolved from the FPL API: true if any of the three has a chance_of_playing below 100 at the Gameweek 6 deadline.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-081,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is Calibrator worth more to me as a decision tool than as a calibration record?,Most questions pair a forecast with a high and low action.,optimise sessions for decisions,optimise them for scorable forecasts,synthesis,75,60,78,60,80,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note states which use mattered.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-016,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will I regret dropping all four learning projects by this time next year?,91% that agent work teaches their skills; 18% that I build any.,keep the compiler project alive,leave all four dropped,calibration,75,60,75,85,72,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note expresses regret or relief about the dropped projects.,2027-10-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-083,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Should every todo carry a date and a done-condition, now that the vague 'Wildcard' item took a week to decode?",'Wildcard' due 8 October meant the FPL chip (100%).,require a date and a done-condition on every todo,leave todos free-form,synthesis,72,65,72,60,78,exploit,Resolved true if every #todo note added 2026-10-03 to 2026-10-31 has a date and a done-condition.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-038,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will removing a CLAUDE.md shim break skill discovery in at least one of my repositories?,"Claude Code reads AGENTS.md as a fallback, but not skills in .agents/skills.",test one repository before removing the rest,remove them all at once,news,70,65,72,70,75,exploit,Resolved true if a later commit restores a CLAUDE.md or reports a missing skill after a shim removal.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-077,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Are my answers too easy to be informative, since none sat near 50?",Nothing at 50; 31 answers at or beyond 15 or 85.,ask for harder questions that sit closer to 50,keep the current difficulty,calibration,75,55,75,72,80,exploit,"Resolved by session 2's export: true if fewer than 10 answers fall between 35 and 65.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-047,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Do the question ids in my #calibrator notes make them less useful as notes?,Each of today's 20 notes cites ids such as cal-20261002-011.,drop ids from future notes and rely on raw.toon,keep the ids,project,70,55,85,60,80,exploit,Resolved by the format of the next session's #calibrator notes.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-094,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would writing my ten-year goal in one paragraph change this week's stop-doing list?,21% that a six-month compression changes this week's work; the stop list is new.,write the paragraph before the 9 October review,keep working opportunistically,calibration,70,60,65,78,72,explore,Resolved by a later note stating the goal and whether the list changed; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-080,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would a resolution pass on session-1 questions before session 3 change how much I trust my credences?,Several session-1 questions resolve by mid-October from the FPL API and repositories.,run a resolution pass before session 3,wait for more horizons,calibration,75,55,72,55,78,exploit,Resolved true if raw.toon has at least one question with resolution_status resolved by session 3's export.,third session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-067,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Do I need a week of logged bedtimes to choose the right curfew hour?,No sleep data is recorded.,log bedtimes for a week before choosing the curfew,set the curfew without data,synthesis,70,60,72,68,72,explore,Resolved by a later note reporting a week of bedtimes; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-082,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is the weekly Calibrator session replacing my need for a separate weekly review?,The stop-doing list adds its own weekly review.,drop the separate review,keep both,synthesis,65,60,72,65,75,exploit,Resolved true if no separate weekly review note appears in October while sessions continue.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-079,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will I answer session 3 within seven days of this one?,71% that I still answer weekly by mid-November.,keep a weekly cadence,move to fortnightly,calibration,65,60,55,60,82,exploit,Resolved true if raw.toon holds a third session exported by 2026-10-09.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-042,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Could I state last month's agent spend within a day if asked?,30% that spend exceeds the site work's value; no spend figure is in my notes.,keep spend as it is,set up a monthly spend summary,notes,65,60,72,68,72,explore,Resolved true if a later note states a monthly agent spend figure.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-063,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is the motives-and-periods visual the one new visualisation this month I would actually use?,82% that it teaches more than another note.,make it the only new visual this month,build it alongside others,synthesis,65,60,72,70,70,explore,Resolved true if it is the only visualisation catalogued in October and a note cites it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-051,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will I open the Convexity Action Engine at least three times before 31 October?,"35% that I use it before starting work: my most uncertain answer.",keep it in the catalogue,retire it,calibration,72,55,60,70,72,explore,Resolved by a later note citing the tool at least three times; unresolved if none.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-030,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"If my rank after Gameweek 10 is worse than after Gameweek 5, will I play FPL less actively?",I gave 24% to an improved rank.,set a rank threshold now that ends active play,keep playing regardless,notes,60,60,75,70,72,explore,Resolved by later FPL notes after Gameweek 10; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-071,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Do I need a 'parked until <date>' state for things like VGC, besides 'dropped' and 'resolved'?","VGC is paused until November, not dropped.",add a parked state with a date,keep two states,synthesis,65,55,78,55,72,exploit,Resolved true if data/notes.md uses a parked or equivalent dated state by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-068,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will a job or contract I want in the next six months ask for a certificate?,Certificates are on the stop list at 84% that repositories signal better.,keep one certificate as an option,drop certificates,calibration,65,55,65,75,68,explore,Resolved by a later note on an application that asks for a certificate; unresolved otherwise.,2027-04-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-049,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would a 'start here' list of my three best pages serve a visitor better than the full catalogue?,"55 visualisations, 17 blog posts, 5 media items.",add a start-here list of three,leave navigation as it is,project,60,60,72,60,70,explore,Resolved true if the site home page links a three-item start list by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-058,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will one engineer's feedback make me reverse the beamdiag feature freeze before 2 November?,Freeze endorsed at 92%; feedback at 100%.,plan the next feature from the feedback,keep the freeze to 2 November,calibration,65,55,65,60,72,exploit,Resolved true if yujieteo/beamdiag gains a feat commit between 2026-10-03 and 2026-11-02.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-031,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is a Chelsea double worth it despite Palmer and João Pedro both at 75% fitness?,Chelsea face one fixture rated above difficulty 3 in their next eight.,double up on Chelsea,avoid Chelsea,news,55,65,60,55,75,exploit,"Resolved from FPL API: true if Chelsea's two highest-owned attackers average over 5 points per gameweek across Gameweeks 6-8.",2026-10-25,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-050,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would a blog post on what session 1 changed help me more than its 20 notes?,Notes are atomic; posts are where I synthesise.,write the post,leave it as notes,synthesis,60,55,72,55,70,explore,Resolved true if a blog post about Calibrator results is published by 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-032,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is Bogle a better defender pick than a second Arsenal defender for Gameweeks 6-8?,"Bogle: £4.6m, form 11.3, 7.2% owned.",buy Bogle,buy a second Arsenal defender,news,55,60,60,55,72,exploit,Resolved from FPL API points over Gameweeks 6-8 against the highest-owned Arsenal defender other than Raya.,2026-10-25,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-100,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will one specific question to the engineer get more useful feedback than asking what they think?,"Open requests for feedback often get politeness, not information.",ask one specific question about the hand calculations,ask for general feedback,synthesis,60,55,65,50,72,exploit,"Resolved by the recorded beamdiag feedback: true if it answers a specific question; unresolved if none.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-055,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will a non-flagged browser call any of my site's WebMCP tools by 30 June 2027?,The origin trial runs to Chrome 156; no token is registered.,keep adding tools to every visual,stop adding tools,news,60,55,65,60,68,explore,Resolved true if a later note or log shows a WebMCP tool call from a non-flagged browser by 2027-06-30.,2027-06-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-062,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will I spend the information-cohomology afternoon before November?,"Endorsed at 82%, with a deadline of 31 December.",book the afternoon now,leave it for December,calibration,60,55,55,55,68,exploit,Resolved true if a note on information cohomology is dated by 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-086,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is amending the grilling skill this week worth more than any single new skill?,Seven skills added in five days; the amendment is still open.,amend grilling before adding a skill,add skills as needs arise,calibration,55,55,55,60,70,exploit,Resolved true if yujieteo/skills changes grilling before adding any new skill after 2026-10-02.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-099,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Has noncommutative geometry already been dropped in practice, though I chose to keep it?","Seven NCG notes on 25 September, none since; 19% that it goes first.",put NCG on the stop list explicitly,schedule one NCG note this month,calibration,60,50,60,72,65,exploit,Resolved true if no noncommutative-geometry note appears between 2026-10-03 and 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-085,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would a weaker model as devil's advocate on one weekly decision change it at least once this month?,18% earlier; my note says flawed analysis forces scrutiny.,run a weak-model critique on one decision a week,keep strong models only,notes,60,50,60,70,65,explore,Resolved by a later note reporting such a trial; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-093,cal-2026-10-02-s2,"Is laddering, not reading, also the better way to learn FPL, via a mini-league against friends?",88% for laddering over reading in VGC; FPL is played alone.,join or start a mini-league with people I know,keep playing alone,synthesis,55,50,72,55,68,explore,Resolved true if a later note mentions a mini-league with people I know.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-057,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will an engineer value beamdiag's hand-calculation export more than its diagrams?,"Hand calcs, units, NASTRAN export and narrated decks were added in three days.",lead the message with the hand calculations,lead with the diagrams,project,55,50,65,50,70,explore,Resolved by the recorded engineer feedback; unresolved if none.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-044,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will at least one crewmate this month act on a false premise in its brief?,15% that false premises already bite; briefs are taken as true.,audit three recent briefs for false premises,skip the audit,notes,55,55,50,60,65,explore,Resolved by a later note reporting a false-premise failure or an audit finding none.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-084,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will the 27 todos closed without answers stay closed with no outcome note by 30 November?,23% that closing them hid exploration debt.,reopen the three that matter as dated todos,let them stay closed,calibration,60,45,45,70,70,exploit,Resolved true if none of the 27 items gains an outcome or dropped reason by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-092,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will the daily first-hand note produce at least one note I would still keep in a year?,Seven notes from 3 to 9 October.,keep the practice after the week,stop after seven days,calibration,55,50,55,50,70,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later review keeps or discards them.,2027-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-064,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would asking an agent to formalise one étale statement in Lean teach me something about the statement?,16% when it would cost me two hours; an agent could do it alone.,try it once this month,skip Lean,news,60,45,70,60,62,explore,Resolved true if a Lean file formalising a statement from my notes is committed by 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-078,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Should the next session drop VGC questions while VGC is on the stop list?,This session asks only one VGC question.,drop VGC from generation until November,keep a few VGC questions,calibration,55,50,50,45,72,exploit,Resolved by the next session's count of VGC questions.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-053,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will the site's Python suite stay under half its 600-second CI budget through October without pruning?,f650447's CI run took about four minutes in all.,trust the budget,schedule another pruning pass,calibration,55,50,55,55,65,exploit,Resolved true if no commit between 2026-10-03 and 2026-10-31 removes tests citing CI time.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-096,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will Brighton's attack keep scoring three or more in at least two of Gameweeks 6-8?,Brighton scored three or more in four of the first five gameweeks.,add a second Brighton attacker,stay at one Brighton attacker,news,50,55,55,45,68,exploit,"Resolved from Gameweek 6-8 results: true if Brighton score three or more in at least two.",2026-10-25,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-018,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would cutting the site's per-visualisation logic tests to smoke checks lose a regression I would notice?,"Re-ask: 21% on a swapped card.",keep the logic tests,cut to smoke checks,calibration,55,50,55,60,60,exploit,Resolved by a later commit or note recording a regression a removed test would have caught; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-069,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will I touch option pricing again before April 2027 anyway?,"Dropped at 82%, but the Breeden–Litzenberger and convex-payoff visuals stay public.",keep one finance note as a parking place,drop it fully,calibration,55,45,60,65,60,explore,Resolved true if a #finance note other than FPL appears by 2027-04-01.,2027-04-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-095,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would answering the top 25 at a desk rather than on a phone change my answers?,Session 1 took 17 minutes in one sitting.,answer the top 25 at a desk,keep answering anywhere,project,50,45,70,45,65,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note compares the two.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-087,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Will the 'dropped' convention land in the notes playbook by 31 October?,Endorsed at 84%; the playbook says to close todos as resolved.,keep the deadline,add it now while it is fresh,calibration,50,45,45,50,65,exploit,Resolved true if skills/playbooks/add-note.md mentions a dropped state by 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-059,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Should beamdiag hide narrated decks and the NASTRAN export until someone asks for them?,A first-time engineer sees every feature at once.,hide advanced features from the first view,keep everything visible,project,45,45,60,50,60,explore,Resolved true if beamdiag's first view hides those features by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-019,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Would deleting the token-reduction tools I no longer use lose me anything?,"Re-ask: 22% on a swapped card.",keep them,delete them,calibration,45,45,45,55,55,exploit,Resolved by a later note recording which tools were kept; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s2-020,cal-2026-10-02-s2,Is a WebMCP safety-evaluation harness worth building before any agent calls my tools?,"Re-ask: 30% on a swapped card.",build the evaluation now,defer it,calibration,45,45,45,55,55,explore,Resolved true if a WebMCP evaluation harness is committed by 2026-12-31.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T05:10:00Z"
